   {
    "id": "p_00006",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     3
    ],
    "text": "The [I5]signal[/I5]() function chooses one of three ways in which receipt of the signal number [I6]sig[/I6] is to be subsequently\nhandled. If the value of [I7]func[/I7] is SIG_DFL, default handling for that signal shall occur. If the value of [I8]func[/I8] is\nSIG_IGN, the signal shall be ignored. Otherwise, the application shall ensure that [I9]func[/I9] points to a function to be called\nwhen that signal occurs. An invocation of such a function because of a signal, or (recursively) of any further functions called by\nthat invocation (other than functions in the standard library), is called a &quot;signal handler&quot;.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I5": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I6": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I7": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I8": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I9": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00007",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     5
    ],
    "text": "When a signal occurs, and [I10]func[/I10] points to a function, it is implementation-defined whether the equivalent of a:",
    "placeholders": {
     "I10": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00008",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     9
    ],
    "text": "is executed or the implementation prevents some implementation-defined set of signals (at least including [I11]sig[/I11]) from\noccurring until the current signal handling has completed. (If the value of [I12]sig[/I12] is SIGILL, the implementation may\nalternatively define that no action is taken.) Next the equivalent of:",
    "placeholders": {
     "I11": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I12": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00009",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     13
    ],
    "text": "is executed. If and when the function returns, if the value of [I13]sig[/I13] was SIGFPE, SIGILL, or SIGSEGV or any other\nimplementation-defined value corresponding to a computational exception, the behavior is undefined. Otherwise, the program shall\nresume execution at the point it was interrupted. The ISO&nbsp;C standard places a restriction on applications relating to the use\nof [A14][I15]raise[/I15]()[/A14] from signal handlers. [S16][[A17]CX[/A17]][/S16] [IMG18] &nbsp;This\nrestriction does not apply to POSIX applications, as POSIX.1-2024 requires [A19][I20]raise[/I20]()[/A19] to\nbe async-signal-safe (see [A21][I22]2.4.3 Signal Actions[/I22][/A21]). [IMG23]",
    "placeholders": {
     "I13": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A14": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/raise.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I15": {
      "open": "<i>",
