   {
    "id": "p_00033",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     41,
     1
    ],
    "text": "The [A101][I102]sigaction[/I102]()[/A101] function provides a more comprehensive and reliable mechanism\nfor controlling signals; new applications should use [A103][I104]sigaction[/I104]()[/A103] rather than\n[I105]signal[/I105]().",
    "placeholders": {
     "A101": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/sigaction.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I102": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A103": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/sigaction.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I104": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I105": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00034",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     43
    ],
    "text": "[A106][/A106]RATIONALE",
    "placeholders": {
     "A106": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_552_08\" id=\"tag_17_552_08\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00035",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     45,
     1
    ],
    "text": "The ISO&nbsp;C standard says that the use of [I107]signal[/I107]() in a multi-threaded program results in undefined behavior. However,\nPOSIX.1 has required [I108]signal[/I108]() to be thread-safe since before threads were added to the ISO&nbsp;C standard.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I107": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I108": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00036",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     47
    ],
